My dwarven arch (XL 15 now) is about going to collect any nightmarish
situations I ever could imagine! Not enough, that he suffered from
lycanthropy in the early game (first time I survived that!) and
teleportitis (even did the quest with it plus a pet dragon and no magic
whistle)and now, on Dlvl 22 it became even more weird: He found a new ring
there, dipped into holy water and hopefully tried a controlled teleport,
but - nothing. Unfortunately he forgot to remove that unid'd ring again. A
fatal mistake, as it turned out to be a =oPolymorph and changed poor
Rubinstein into a cockatrice! Imagine a cockatrice on Dlvl 22 with
teleportitis... The first moves (and jumps) weren't not so bad - the whole
level slowly filled up with nice statues and the cockatrice's archeologist
heart was going to beat faster.

Unfortunately the whole level was not only filled up with statues, also
with monsters. Lots of elves appeared, with remarkable interest in
Rubinstein's pile. Thanks to his intrinsics (already crowned), all his
wands of cold, preferably zapped by the elves, couldn't harm him. But then
(imagine a big, ugly grin from the RNG) a leather golem appeared!
Rubinstein tried to prevent a direct fight, since he didn't know how those
golems would deal with stoning attacks. Basically a wise decision, as
should turn out later...

The next problem: Hunger! What kind of food does a cockatrice need? And
how does he hunt for food when everything he touch immediately turns to
stone? Looting the BoH from the pile was no option, but fortunately (and
ironically) Rubinstein always left some spare lizard corpses outside a
container - precaution against cockatrice attacks... ;-)

But hunger came back very soon, poor cockatrice got weak... then
fainting...
and then his old friend, the lether golem stepped in. Here Rubinstein
decided better to die in honour and attacked the golem. The leather golem
turned to - a stone golem! Eeech, that's the real nightmare for a
cockatrice! In the very next moment Rubinstein turned back to his original
form, naked and still fainting. So, as a last resource, a prayer must
help, regardless of the bad conscience about killing some friendly tengus
before...

The (happy) end of the story is: The prayer worked, Rubinstein was able to
retreat from the stone golem straight to his pile and picked up his +5
Excalibur. There was no armor left but fortunately his BoH with the
mattock in it. Then Rubinstein started chipping the statues...
"Aah, here is my dwarvish mithril coat, my speed boots, my... EVERYTHING!"
___________________

No matter how and when this game will end: It's already the most thrilling one I
ever played!

